{
  "id": "tallis-canon",
  "name": "Tallis' Canon",
  "source": "Thomas Tallis, the eighth of the nine tunes he wrote for Matthew Parker's The Whole Psalter Translated into English Metre, c. 1567, and known as THE EIGHTH TUNE before it was known by his name. Melody transcribed from the ABC setting at abc.musicaviva.com (tallis-thomas/tallis-canon, transcribed by Frank Nordberg) and checked against the Hymnary incipit for TALLIS' CANON, 11711 22314 43322, which it matches note for note. Public domain: the melody only, never a modern harmonisation. The second voice here is the first delayed by one bar and wrapped at the loop point -- which is what the tune is, a canon at the octave one bar apart, rather than a thirty-two-note melody with a tail.",
